From 89747d565fcf14191796dc47db24e1334b4389d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kamil Monicz <kamil@monicz.dev>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:44:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] numpy: Add fallible array construction and ownership transfer

Return Python construction errors through additive APIs while keeping existing infallible constructors and third-party IntoPyArray implementations source-compatible. Keep Rust owners alive until array creation succeeds, check null before assigning the base, and propagate base-assignment errors without releasing a stolen reference twice.

Exercise deterministic container, array, zero-allocation and real NumPy base-assignment failures in an isolated test executable. Cover zero-copy numeric vectors, matrix layouts, readonly results and borrowed owners on CPython 3.15 and its free-threaded build.
